      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Assignment timestamps are fixed at module import time",
      "description": "`queued: datetime = timezone.now()` evaluates once when the module is imported, not when an `AssignmentSource` is created. Every instance created without an explicit timestamp therefore carries the worker\u2019s module-import time, potentially hours or days before the assignment. `to_dict()` propagates that incorrect timestamp into queued tasks.\n\nUse `field(default_factory=timezone.now)` and add a test that creates instances at different mocked times and verifies each receives its own creation timestamp.",
